Error case: --group with a --scope other than all is a usage error, exit 2, before any request.
-- args --
segments
leaderboard
a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
--group
4242
--scope
connections
-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
Usage: gccli segments leaderboard <uuid> [flags]

Show the leaderboard of a segment.

Arguments:
  <uuid>    Segment UUID.

Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json              Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain             Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header            Print the column names as the first line of --plain
                          output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"      Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING    Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"      Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                          elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                          auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us, statute_uk
                          ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version           Print version information.

      --from-rank=1       Rank to start at. One page has 26 rows.
      --scope="all"       Whose times: all, connections, following or me.
      --group=ID          Show only the members of this group. Goes only with
                          --scope all.
      --gender=GENDER     Gender: female or male.
      --age=AGES          Age group: 0-18, 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64 or
                          65-120.

gccli: error: segments leaderboard: --group cannot go with --scope connections: a group leaderboard has the times of all its members
